Freerunning and Skating in V
Mirror's Edge parkour and Skate 3 skating in GTA V Legacy story mode.
An unofficial fan project, unaffiliated with EA, DICE, Rockstar Games or Take-Two Interactive.
It contains no Mirror's Edge, Skate 3 or GTA V code or data.

This repository is a fork of SK8V, but SK8V itself is not built or shipped from it: the launcher
downloads becaring's own release from https://github.com/becaring/SK8V and runs his setup tools
from it unchanged. SK8V's own files were removed from this fork's main branch except rust/svwc,
which Faith Runner V uses. They are all in becaring's repository.

This project builds on:

Faith Runner (MIT License)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Tanner. https://github.com/tnrjns/faith-runner
  third_party/faith-runner/crates: faith_move, faith_anim and me_assets, copied from his repository.
  faith_move is changed for GTA's hollow, detailed buildings: a vault needs a top above the wall;
  ledge grabs and pull-ups need a clear way over the lip; a host can mark an obstacle to vault
  right across (World::vault_across, car bonnets); wallclimbs can step out round small overhangs
  (Tuning::overhang_step_out, off by default); springboards can launch off a step into a wall
  (Tuning::springboard_into_walls, off by default), keeping the run-in speed for the wallclimb,
  or off a step at a building's edge, such as a roof's parapet with at least 2 m of drop beyond it
  (Tuning::springboard_into_air, off by default).
  faith_anim has one change: a faster ladder climb (Tuning::ladder_climb_speed) speeds up the arms
  by only its square root. me_assets is unchanged.
  Every change: faithrunner-v/patches/faith-runner-gta-changes.patch. Licence: licenses/faith-runner-LICENSE.txt

